  "coverArt": "Mother Kell, tiny in layered sea-grey shawls, stands at the end of a ruined stone quay with her driftwood stick, milky eyes open. Behind her the whole Gullwake crew towers, baffled. Skarn lies flat at her feet like a dog. Dead village up the hill, shell chimes on every door. Sea-grey, bone white, one warm hearth light.",
